      "title": "UK and EU agree deal to reset ties nearly a decade after Brexit",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-20T11:38:47Z",
      "durationSec": 451,
      "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/YctVHdG2v78/mqdefault.jpg",
      "description": "The UK and European Union have agreed on new measures to strengthen ties nearly a decade after Brexit. Following Prime Minister Andy Burnham's visit to Brussels, the initial agreements cover easier food exports, youth mobility for up to 100,000 people annually and cooperation on carbon emissions. But with legal formalities still to come, questions remain over how much the deals will benefit ordinary Britons, particularly in communities that strongly backed Brexit.\n\nAl Jazeera’s Rosie Birchard and Rory Challon report.\n\nSubscribe to our channel: http://bit.ly/AJSubscribe\nFollow us on Twitter: https://twitter.com/AJEnglish\nFind us on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/aljazeera\nCheck our website: http://www.aljazeera.com/\nCheck out our Instagram page: https://www.instagram.com/aljazeeraenglish/\nDownload AJE Mobile App: https://aje.io/AJEMobile\n\n#aljazeeraenglish #BreakingNews #aljazeeralivenews #aljazeeraenglish   #newsfeed #news #aljazera #latestnews #BreakingNews #news",
